From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: build <build@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 19:06:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt6797: admit the power-save profile command

The join-command encoder admits a fixed list of firmware commands, and the
power-save profile, 0x05, was not on it: on the device 0813's request came
back -EINVAL at once, with nothing sent. Admit it for BSS 0 with a profile of
0, 1 or 2 and its two reserved bytes zero; it stays refused during cleanup,
like every other command but removal and abort. Also stop logging a request
that changes nothing.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c  | 6 ++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
index 8e7978e..98f07fa 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/hif.c
@@ -200,6 +200,12 @@ mt6797_join_prepare_command(struct mt6797_normal_transaction *t,
 	    !t->tc4_limit || t->tc4_limit > 0xffffU || t->tc4_free > t->tc4_limit)
 		return mt6797_normal_abort(t);
 	switch (cid) {
+	case 0x05:
+		/* The power-save profile, BSS 0 only: 0, 1 or 2. */
+		if (bytes != 4 || payload[0] || payload[1] > 2 || payload[2] || payload[3])
+			return -EINVAL;
+		required = 4;
+		break;
 	case 0x07:
 		required = MT6797_JOIN_KEY_BYTES;
 		break;
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
index 90f2066..656f9b6 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mediatek/mt6797/main.c
@@ -1600,10 +1600,10 @@ void mt6797_mac_join_send_ps(struct mt6797_mac *mac)
 	unsigned int profile = mac->ps_wanted ? mac->ps_profile : 0;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (!mac->ps_profile)
+	if (!mac->ps_profile || mac->ps_sent == (int)profile)
 		return;
 	if (!mac->join_data_phase || mac->join_data_ended ||
-	    mac->ps_sent == (int)profile || mac->closing || mac->first_error) {
+	    mac->closing || mac->first_error) {
 		dev_info(wiphy_dev(mac->hw->wiphy),
 			 "one-shot WLAN power save held: profile=%u sent=%d data=%u ended=%u closing=%u first=%d\n",
 			 profile, mac->ps_sent, mac->join_data_phase, mac->join_data_ended,
-- 
